-- title:
--   Galois displacement on ℚₚ(μ_{pⁿ}) bounded by that of ζ
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let `PadicAlgCl p` be the algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}_p$ used throughout, equipped with its canonical extension of the $p$-adic absolute value $\|\cdot\|$. Fix $n \in \mathbb{N}$ and an element $\zeta$ of `PadicAlgCl p` which is a primitive $p^n$-th root of unity, and let $\sigma$ be an automorphism of `PadicAlgCl p` as a $\mathbb{Q}_p$-algebra. Let $y$ be an element of `PadicAlgCl p` lying in [`PadicAlgCl.cyclotomicTower p n`](def/PadicAlgCl_CyclotomicTower.html#L9), that is, in the intermediate field of `PadicAlgCl p` over $\mathbb{Q}_p$ generated by the set of all $\xi$ with $\xi^{p^n} = 1$, and assume $\|y\| \le 1$. The conclusion is the inequality $$\|\sigma y - y\| \le \|\sigma \zeta - \zeta\|.$$ Thus the displacement of $\sigma$ on the whole ring of elements of norm at most $1$ in $\mathbb{Q}_p(\mu_{p^n})$ is controlled by its displacement on a single primitive $p^n$-th root of unity; the bound is stated for the archimedean-style absolute value rather than for a normalised valuation.
--
--   This is the monogenicity step in Serre's computation of the ramification filtration of $\mathbb{Q}_p(\mu_{p^n})/\mathbb{Q}_p$: the ramification function $i(\sigma) = \min\{v(\sigma y - y) : \|y\| \le 1\}$ is attained at the generator $\zeta$ of the ring of integers $\mathbb{Z}_p[\zeta]$. It is used in the derivation of a uniform bound on $\|\sigma y - y\|$ for elements of a join of cyclotomic towers, in [`PadicAlgCl.exists_forall_rpow_neg_lt_norm_algEquiv_sub_of_mem_sup_cyclotomicTower`](thm.html#PadicAlgCl.exists_forall_rpow_neg_lt_norm_algEquiv_sub_of_mem_sup_cyclotomicTower).
